    "body": "`head_size=512` support (and the new NoPE path/quantized-cache rejection for that head size) is introduced here, but the existing sparse-MLA backend tests appear to only exercise the 576/rope=64 configurations. Adding a targeted unit test for FlashMLASparseBackend with `qk_rope_head_dim=0` (so `head_size=kv_lora_rank=512`) would help prevent regressions in backend selection and the `forward_mqa` concat/copy logic.",
